From 83a909306d6b2d9b834d26ddb03cb888ff3af8e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 11:38:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07187/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-6:
 deterministic-router control -- was it ever SGE?

Answers the question left open by the REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-5 corrigendum:
was "0/3 leveled up" evidence against SGE specifically, or evidence
that the stripped-down harness (induction/frame-change-scorer/goal-
bias/go-explore-archive all deliberately disabled to isolate the
router under test) simply can't reach level 1 on these 3 games
regardless of exploration strategy? No prior run in this whole
investigation ever tried a different router under the same config.

scripts/outer_loop_sge_smoke_test.py gains router_mode="baseline"
(run_game) / --baseline (CLI): swaps SGECandidateRouter for exp5534's
own deterministic, zero-LLM BoundedStrategyCandidateRouter under the
IDENTICAL policy config, budget, and games. Writes to non-colliding
paths so SGE-mode artifacts (including g50t's backward-compat path)
are untouched.

Real run: the control ALSO never leaves level 0 on any of the 3 games
(real_initial_level=0, real_max_level_observed=0, leveled_up=false --
confirmed against each raw action_log, not just the summary),
completing in ~2s per game (vs 20-50s for SGE, no LLM invoked) with
44-45 attempts, matching SGE's budget exhaustion. A structurally
different router, zero shared code path beyond rank(), lands on the
exact same result.

This resolves the open question: it was never SGE specifically. The
stripped-down harness is what caps every run in this investigation at
level 0 -- the other disabled production systems appear load-bearing
for even a first level-up on g50t/sk48/cd82 within ~45 actions,
independent of router. Every REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-3/5699-4 "0/3 leveled
up" finding should be read as "this harness configuration can't reach
level 1 with any router tried so far," not "SGE adds no value" --
that comparison genuinely cannot be made from this data. The
router-internal findings (nudge firing, parse-rate improvements,
cd82's advice language shifting correctly) remain true and
independent of this control.

2 new tests (baseline mode uses the real BoundedStrategyCandidateRouter,
spec-declaration). Spec: REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-6 with its own scenario.
Logged in ops/known-issues.md task 6 with the concrete open follow-up
(longer budget, or re-enable the other disabled features, to find out
whether level 1 is reachable here at all).

